penkra tabs snapshot
Capture the current accessibility snapshot of one exact retained App tab.

How to use this operation

References remain valid for the document's current loader and become stale after navigation. Choose d1 for the App document or d2 for its hosted page.

Examples

  Observe one retained tab

  {
    "command": "penkra tabs snapshot --tab-id <tab-id> --document d1 --interactive true --compact true"
  }

Input fields
  --document <string>  required; one of "d1", "d2". d1 addresses the App document; d2 addresses its hosted page, when present.
  --tab-id <string>  required. Exact retained App tab ID returned by penkra tabs list.
  --boxes <boolean>  optional.
  --compact <boolean>  optional.
  --depth <number>  optional.
  --filename <string>  optional.
  --interactive <boolean>  optional.
  --ref <string>  optional. Durable document reference returned by snapshot for the current loader.

Invocation
  Send one ordinary command string. Pass each input field by name exactly as listed
  under Input fields (for example --thread-id <id>). A bare value without its --name
  is rejected. Use --input "{...}" to pass the complete input as one JSON value.
  --input   Complete JSON operation input validated against the schema below.

Operating manual
  Run penkra tabs --help for Tabs operating instructions.

Validated input schema
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "tabId": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1,
      "description": "Exact retained App tab ID returned by penkra tabs list."
    },
    "document": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "d1",
        "d2"
      ],
      "description": "d1 addresses the App document; d2 addresses its hosted page, when present."
    },
    "ref": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^d[12]:e[0-9]+$",
      "description": "Durable document reference returned by snapshot for the current loader."
    },
    "depth": {
      "type": "number",
      "minimum": 0
    },
    "boxes": {
      "type": "boolean"
    },
    "interactive": {
      "type": "boolean"
    },
    "compact": {
      "type": "boolean"
    },
    "filename": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "tabId",
    "document"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}

Validated output schema
{
  "type": "object"
}

penkra tabs act
Run an ordered sequence of actions against d1 and d2.

How to use this operation

Act accepts steps through --input. Activate the tab and take a fresh snapshot first; inactive interaction fails before dispatch. A failed sequence reports completed steps and whether the failing step was dispatched. Element actions use d1:/d2: references from snapshot; --human true uses an eased visible cursor path. Upload targets a file input reference and accepts local file paths; absolute paths use the desktop filesystem and relative paths use the App's storage directory.

Examples

  Click and wait

  {
    "command": "penkra tabs act --input '{\"tabId\":\"<tab-id>\",\"steps\":[{\"action\":\"click\",\"ref\":\"d1:e3\"},{\"action\":\"wait\",\"document\":\"d1\",\"text\":\"Saved\"}]}'"
  }

Input fields
  --steps <array>  required.
  --tab-id <string>  required. Exact retained App tab ID returned by penkra tabs list.
  --human <boolean>  optional.

Invocation
  Send one ordinary command string. Pass each input field by name exactly as listed
  under Input fields (for example --thread-id <id>). A bare value without its --name
